 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "92 is addressed to the Prophet ﷺ («أتوك», «قلت»): no motif there; no tears, people or mounts drawn. 91:7-13 is not glossed: every short excerpt either repeats «لا يجدون» or drops the negation. Light for «غفور رحيم», coins for «ما ينفقون» and «أغنياء», a house for «مع الخوالف». 92, 94: short-word flags, listen. STAGING v4: c1 (91): a town by day. Three believers sit on the left (the weak and the sick who cannot go out: As-Sa'di); a poor man in a patched robe sits on the right (those who find nothing to spend: Al-Muyassar). Nothing is acted on the condition «إذا نصحوا» (91:15-18), the shot is wide while the Messenger is named (91:14 to 91:20); a soft sparkle on them on 91:21 (no blame on the doers of good); a geometric plate from 91:25 (Forgiving, Merciful), starting on the attribute, not on the Name. c2 (92) stays ambient: they came to the Messenger, he answered them and they turned back weeping; staging them would make them speak to and turn away from an empty side that stands for him; the mood moves from dawn to night_sky and the background is quiet over the whole verse; no motif, and no tears, people or mounts drawn; camera moves only. c3 (93): inside a home by day; three men (the rich who asked leave, hypocrites: Al-Muyassar). Their asking the Messenger is not acted; a coins plate on 93:7 (rich), they sit down on 93:10 (staying with those who stay behind), a house plate on 93:11-12 that leaves before the Name; nothing is drawn for the sealing of hearts; the camera holds on them for 93:17-19."
 },
